## Scenario 3: Delayed Downlink — Receiving After Delay
##
## ION starts up and is ready to receive.
## The LTP peer (node 20) does not begin transmitting until +30 seconds.
## After 30s, bundles arrive from the satellite and are delivered locally.
##
## This demonstrates receiving bundles from a peer that becomes available
## after startup (e.g., satellite rises above horizon).

1 10 ''
s

# Self-contact
a contact +0 +86400 10 10 100000000

# Terrestrial link (node 30) — available immediately
a contact +0 +86400 10 30 100000000
a contact +0 +86400 30 10 100000000

# Satellite link (node 20) — DELAYED: peer starts sending at +30s
# Outbound available immediately (we can queue), inbound arrives after +30s
a contact +0 +86400 10 20 9600
a contact +30 +86400 20 10 9600

# Ranges
a range +0 +86400 10 10 0
a range +0 +86400 10 20 1
a range +0 +86400 20 10 1
a range +0 +86400 10 30 0
a range +0 +86400 30 10 0
